// TownLab decorations per building (generated by Tools/townlab_decor.py, 2026-11-14; edit that script, not this file).
// Every piece sits in its building's own frame: X along its length, Y with the door side at +Y, Z up, cm, the model's
// floor at Z 0, as /Game/TownLab/Buildings/SM_TL_<Name> is drawn before its FModel Scale (OakHill.h). Place():
//   bScaleWithBuilding (ivy, moss, the lanterns): the building's whole transform, Scale included, as if attached to it;
//   otherwise (props, stones, weeds) the spot moves with the building's Scale but the piece keeps its own Scale (real size).
// Mesh: a full asset path, or a name in /Game/TownLab/Buildings. bLight: a spot for a real light (lanterns, about 25 cm below).
// bCastShadow: false for the small pieces and the ivy and moss cards (speed rules, Docs/TownLab/StyleSheet.md).
#pragma once
#include "CoreMinimal.h"

